From: CanMehEvolve <noreply@example.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] MesgDefinition::GetFieldByIndex: raw data pointer and branch
 hint

What: uses fields.data() and a __builtin_expect hint for the in-range case.
Why it might be faster: removes the vector operator[] indirection; effect is tiny (0.16% at search time) and within noise. __builtin_expect is a GCC/Clang extension.

Provenance: greedy search, seed 3, generation 28, region 555 (MesgDefinition::GetFieldByIndex).
Generated by the model (deepseek-v4.1-flash); not hand-written. Search-time ratio R (candidate/stock, <1 is faster): 0.8650 -> 0.8635 at acceptance (max of two measurements). This is a ranking value, NOT an independent per-patch
confirmation; only the fixed FINAL patch of the run was re-measured independently.
Cumulative patch it was derived from: runs/deepseek/greedy-s3-1072869/patches/gen_28.patch (diff against stock; do not apply together with the others).
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/fit_mesg_definition.cpp | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/fit_mesg_definition.cpp b/src/fit_mesg_definition.cpp
index 16cad13..14265e0 100644
--- a/src/fit_mesg_definition.cpp
+++ b/src/fit_mesg_definition.cpp
@@ -107,8 +107,11 @@ FieldDefinition* MesgDefinition::GetField(const FIT_UINT8 fieldNum)
 
 FieldDefinition* MesgDefinition::GetFieldByIndex(const FIT_UINT16 index)
 {
-    if (index < fields.size())
-        return &(fields[index]);
+    FieldDefinition* const fieldsData = fields.data();
+    const auto fieldCount = fields.size();
+
+    if (__builtin_expect(index < fieldCount, 1))
+        return fieldsData + index;
 
     return FIT_NULL;
 }
